The data-quality checks (`check_missingness`, `check_constant_columns`, `check_outliers_zscore`, `check_flatline`) take lists as arrays, and the numeric ones raise a `TypeError` for complex values. `check_missingness` reported any list, NaN included, as an empty dataset, and the constant-column check found nothing in one. Complex input was cast to its real part, so a signal held in its imaginary part read as constant and flatlined, and its outliers were missed.
